ncipales herramientas o métodos utilizados para el diagnóstico o tamizaje de fragilidad en la práctica clínica","guid":"zOfOn8DLQruWGM8Y53D5ow","children":[]},{"id":"175","parent":"170","text":"5. Explique las principales intervenciones recomendadas para el manejo de la fragilidad, destacando el rol del ejercicio, la nutrición y la revisión de medicamentos","guid":"Cf9f65Z5SfiGk5-JrwtzxA","children":[]},{"id":"176","parent":"170","text":"6. ¿Qué herramienta de tamizaje de fragilidad sería la más apropiada en su contexto laboral y por qué?","guid":"7G06YMnqT4mcFk2j-mIc_A","children":[]}]},{"id":"177","parent":"0","text":"Evidencia complementaria (papers oficiales)","guid":"wkAu-qIMS2-xdmA5iHdfRg","children":[{"id":"178","parent":"177","text":"Kim & Rockwood NEJM 2024 → revisión narrativa de referencia (concepto, modelos, manejo)","guid":"dpY61BWrQ8SasQREopAZ-A","children":[]},{"id":"179","parent":"177","text":"Orkaby Ann Intern Med 2026 (ITC) → algoritmo clínico actualizado para APS","guid":"9WXJGFQVQhKO7r5hP9KxJQ","children":[]},{"id":"180","parent":"177","text":"Álvarez-Bustos JNHA 2026 (consenso CIBERFES) → conceptualización, detección y manejo multidisciplinario","guid":"NGs_uJq6SvO4aLXQTv5olA","children":[]},{"id":"181","parent":"177","text":"Turner & Clegg Age Ageing 2024 (BGS/Age UK) → mejor evidencia para prevención y manejo en UK","guid":"kefd22pWTLuk0ASBTq7qbQ","children":[]},{"id":"182","parent":"177","text":"Liau JAMDA 2021 → consenso de manejo farmacológico en frágiles (deprescripción + STOPP/START)","guid":"Fgr2DRBiR3CwKfUVy-Iwxg","children":[]},{"id":"183","parent":"177","text":"Javed JGIM 2024 → fragilidad modifica el efecto de las intervenciones en RCTs (revisión sistemática)","guid":"jtQBpGCTRd2V3j8Vf6fE7Q","children":[]},{"id":"184","parent":"177","text":"Huang Int J Nurs Stud 2024 → metaanálisis: VGI hospitalaria mejora AVD y reduce mortalidad","guid":"73VmBe2lQ0CjcKY8mer1cw","children":[]},{"id":"185","parent":"177","text":"Hoogendijk Arch Gerontol Geriatr 2024 → paradoja riesgo-tratamiento: frágiles reciben MENOS terapia recomendada que la justificada por su riesgo","guid":"XzOXQoevS9GFePNQwW4HyQ","children":[]}]},{"id":"186","parent":"0","text":"Perlas Clínicas","guid":"PoGlZqphTzKaVCPIGUoRgg","children":[{"id":"187","parent":"186","text":"Perla 1: El que \"se ve bien\" y no tolera nada es el frágil → respuesta desproporcionada al estrés","guid":"gOKPEeMPQ7-qo0X5eqmPzA","children":[]},{"id":"188","parent":"186","text":"Perla 2: Fragilidad ≠ comorbilidad ≠ dependencia → la VGI los distingue, no usar uno como proxy del otro","guid":"b3ulmdvnTk2OwacOrDhk5A","children":[]},{"id":"189","parent":"186","text":"Perla 3: La fragilidad es REVERSIBLE → NNT 3,2 con paquete multimodal, pocas intervenciones geriátricas tienen ese NNT","guid":"MiGV9tIpSjCooFTm6-iQ_w","children":[]},{"id":"190","parent":"186","text":"Perla 4: FRAIL en 30 s en APS, CFS en hospital y cirugía → no tener herramienta NO es excusa","guid":"h9TZAcqFSoOWc-NYRhDYeg","children":[]},{"id":"191","parent":"186","text":"Perla 5: Velocidad de marcha >5 s en 4 m = bandera roja independiente","guid":"ogbnTXggQjOiTBSWwxKDhQ","children":[]},{"id":"192","parent":"186","text":"Perla 6: Ejercicio ≥3 meses, 2-3 ×/sem, ≥45 min → la dosis importa; VIVIFRAIL listo para prescribir","guid":"wC6mnKtaQnOyHhx1kE1c_Q","children":[]},{"id":"193","parent":"186","text":"Perla 7: Proteína 1,2-1,5 g/kg/día fragmentada en 3 comidas (20-40 g c/u) → el bolo estimula síntesis muscular","guid":"YvXt2CLWRyy4VKpQ7UZjIQ","children":[]},{"id":"194","parent":"186","text":"Perla 8: Sin ejercicio la nutrición no rinde → combo obligatorio kinesiología + nutricionista","guid":"SK4Akci7S6inln7bkgh1Ug","children":[]},{"id":"195","parent":"186","text":"Perla 9: CFS modifica decisiones quirúrgicas/oncológicas → predice mortalidad postop independiente del riesgo basal","guid":"CCTVTWTBSvWdluO7ystpgA","children":[]},{"id":"196","parent":"186","text":"Perla 10: Pérdida de redundancia explica descompensaciones (ej. Na+ con ICC+IR+SIADH) → anticipar al sumar fármacos","guid":"9ow2b4a5RqSA59Dn_IJYKA","children":[]},{"id":"197","parent":"186","text":"Perla 11: Paradoja riesgo-tratamiento (Hoogendijk) → frágiles reciben menos terapia preventiva que la indicada → no negarles intervenciones por edad/CFS sin VGI previa","guid":"sHdWNbHhSpSumi-uLeQDAg","children":[]}]},{"id":"198","parent":"0","text":"Conceptos examinados (Evaluaciones SGGCh 2026)","guid":"0DlJTIixRdSkUUHUPy8tQA","children":[{"id":"199","parent":"198","text":"Evaluacion M2","guid":"TvIm0AlVQA6-1sxnWFtggQ","children":[{"id":"200","parent":"199","text":"P2 (proteinas AM): rango 1,2-1,6 g/kg/dia preserva masa muscular -> superar 0,8 g/kg del adulto joven por resistencia anabolica","guid":"GF0iKBH8TdyEemFRmgd4zQ","children":[]},{"id":"201","parent":"199","text":"P11 (proteinas en fragil): consenso PROT-AGE/ESPEN -> 1,2-1,5 g/kg/dia en fragil o enfermedad aguda; hasta 2,0 g/kg/dia salvo ERC sin dialisis","guid":"TUhToTLvTM-cblgI8UEyGA","children":[]},{"id":"202","parent":"199","text":"P12 (intervencion mayor evidencia): ejercicio multicomponente (fuerza + resistencia + equilibrio + flexibilidad) -> unica intervencion validada para revertir fragilidad; VIVIFRAIL es el programa estructurado en Chile","guid":"wn4XlExJQRKpQJ_TVdK0MA","children":[]},{"id":"203","parent":"199","text":"P14 (ejercicio mayor impacto AVD): entrenamiento de fuerza progresivo -> estimulo mTOR directo, previene sarcopenia (principal causa de perdida autonomia)","guid":"2n9ls-haQg2d2XtVfzc3GQ","children":[]},{"id":"204","parent":"199","text":"P16 (FR fragilidad): polifarmacia es FR independiente -> integrar Beers/STOPP-START a la revision rutinaria","guid":"vYg2hs2rQDGrgQ_HwrX21g","children":[]}]},{"id":"205","parent":"198","text":"Evaluacion Final (transversales)","guid":"vG0U5gXtR6-8dsTQlt2yYg","children":[{"id":"206","parent":"205","text":"P7 (FR fragilidad): polifarmacia confirmada como FR -> deprescripcion forma parte del manejo","guid":"SJdxBSoZQOSEYRc0WqqYdg","children":[]},{"id":"207","parent":"205","text":"P9 (intervencion mayor evidencia): ejercicio multicomponente vuelve a ser respuesta -> reforzar prescripcion estructurada (no caminar 15 min)","guid":"Zig_QBghQH--Tgk3URrqlw","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"208","parent":"0","text":"Referencias (bibliografía oficial Dra. Carrasco)","guid":"PYF8aG6cRtu8UQYyUMHHqw","children":[{"id":"209","parent":"208","text":"1. Kim DH, Rockwood K. Frailty in older adults. N Engl J Med. 2024;391(6):538-548. doi:10.1056/NEJMra2301292","guid":"PXp1Xf5dTY2p7Ll01UAsHQ","children":[]},{"id":"210","parent":"208","text":"2. Orkaby AR, Schwartz AW, Callahan KE. Frailty. Ann Intern Med. 2026;179(2):ITC17-ITC32. doi:10.7326/ANNALS-25-04412","guid":"5N038_KIQsazRXU-GpYhTQ","children":[]},{"id":"211","parent":"208","text":"3. Álvarez-Bustos A, Andres-Lacueva C, Ara I, et al. Consensus document on frailty: conceptualization, detection, multidisciplinary management and future roadmap. J Nutr Health Aging. 2026;30(3):100793. doi:10.1016/j.jnha.2026.100793","guid":"QGQlxB4fRVKfMH7kxmdtkw","children":[]},{"id":"212","parent":"208","text":"4. Turner G, Clegg A. Best evidence for the prevention and management of frailty. Age Ageing. 2024;53(2):afae011. doi:10.1093/ageing/afae011","guid":"7GsPNHCQSeqNa35dv-Cw8A","children":[]},{"id":"213","parent":"208","text":"5. Liau SJ, Lalic S, Sluggett JK, Cesari M, Onder G, Vetrano DL, et al. Medication management in frail older people. J Am Med Dir Assoc. 2021;22(1):43-49. doi:10.1016/j.jamda.2020.05.004","guid":"rGdCYs4eTX-y2R7xrlfUxQ","children":[]},{"id":"214","parent":"208","text":"6. Javed A, et al. Frailty as an effect modifier in randomized controlled trials: A systematic review. J Gen Intern Med. 2024;39:1452-1473. doi:10.1007/s11606-024-08732-8","guid":"WL-gdTDmTiafIEOP5VDqYg","children":[]},{"id":"215","parent":"208","text":"7. Huang XX, et al. The effectiveness of the comprehensive geriatric assessment for older adults with frailty in hospital settings: A systematic review and meta-analysis. Int J Nurs Stud. 2024;159:104849. doi:10.1016/j.ijnurstu.2024.104849","guid":"9XAmFz_6SViDuSJCuZmmGw","children":[]},{"id":"216","parent":"208","text":"8. Hoogendijk EO, et al. Beyond clinical practice guidelines: The risk-treatment paradox in frail older adults. Arch Gerontol Geriatr. 2024;119:105369. doi:10.1016/j.archger.2024.105369","guid":"ZU1ww1SATrKerDu5bA0aIA","children":[]}]}]},"node_count":216,"relations":[],"cross_references":[],"specialty":"Geriatría","folder":"Entidades clínicas/Geriatría","filename":"TIROTOXICOSIS EN ANCIANOS-2025","id":"map_159","resolved_references":[]}